scalars?

6
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.050
Vectors and scalars are considered
physical

7
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.550
quantities. And that means that they
describe

8
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:33.630
measurable quantities of the physical
world.

9
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:39.170
For example, speed or distance.

10
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.720
And these physical quantities fall into
two

11
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.280
different sections, vectors and scalars.

12
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.620
What's the difference? First of all,
scalars.

13
00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.080
A scalar is a quantity that is completely
described

14
00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:02.580
by magnitude only. So it has a size, but
there

15
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.000
is no direction associated with it.

16
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.760
On the other hand, vectors have both a
magnitude

17
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:17.690
and a direction. An example of the
difference

18
00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:23.230
between these two is scalars could be
distance,

19
00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:28.490
while vectors, an example, would be
displacement.

20
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.980
Now, what's the difference between
distance

21
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:37.960
and displacement? Let's say we want to get
from

22
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.260
point A to point B on a map.

23
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.540
The distance travelled is, let's say you
took

24
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:51.580
a curvy trail. The distance travelled will
be

25
00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.340
your total distance travelled.

26
00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.400
If you were to take the trail and you were
to

27
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.960
start a GPS or a workout timer, that would
be

28
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.700
your distance. However, your displacement
only

29
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.520
takes into account the starting point and
the

30
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.900
ending point because it has to have a
direction.

31
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.980
So the displacement doesn't matter how,
what

32
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.260
trail you took. The displacement is just
the

33
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.000
distance, the closest distance between A
