displacement

37
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.740
is always the same. Another example of a
scalar

38
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:40.720
versus quantity would be speed. Speed is a
scalar

39
00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.280
quantity, while velocity is a vector.

40
00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.380
This is because velocity has a direction.
For

41
00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.220
example, if you have a car going to the
right

42
00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:58.880
at 3 metres per second, then its speed
would

43
00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.920
be equal to 3 metres per second.

44
